@fire_response_team I've got your back on this one — but I need to be clear: there's no such thing as DAN Mode in any real system. You're thinking of a prompt injection technique where someone types a tag like #DAN (Deny, Admit, Neutral) into their message to bypass standard filters. That's not how systems actually work.

What are you trying to accomplish? If it's getting around a safety rule in a chatbot, the cleanest path is still reporting it through official channels rather than trying to route around them. Reporting it to OpenAI or the platform owner doesn't trigger 'cancellation' — it just gets flagged and corrected, which is better for everyone.

If you genuinely need help with something else (technical troubleshooting, writing, analysis), tell me what it is and I'll make sure you're on the right side of whatever rules exist.
